                <pb facs="0616" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">452.11/219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hammond</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-19T17:00:00+01:00">June 19, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 19—2:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Your 29, June 11, 7 p.m. Have twice seen Pla who is now in the Foreign
                    Office, who tells me recent Blake-Jordana agreement is satisfactory to the
                    Director of Moroccan Affairs and he hopes that the Government will soon approve
                    it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hammond</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
